  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9807282v4</id>
    <title>Level Spacing Distribution of Critical Random Matrix Ensembles</title>
    <updated>1998-10-17T00:32:09Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9807282v4" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/9807282v4" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We consider unitary invariant random matrix ensembles which obey spectral statistics different from the Wigner-Dyson, including unitary ensembles with slowly (~(log x)^2) growing potentials and the finite-temperature fermi gas model. If the deformation parameters in these matrix ensembles are small, the asymptotically translational-invariant region in the spectral bulk is universally governed by a one-parameter generalization of the sine kernel. We provide an analytic expression for the distribution of the eigenvalue spacings of this universal asymptotic kernel, which is a hybrid of the Wigner-Dyson and the Poisson distributions, by determining the Fredholm determinant of the universal kernel in terms of a Painleve VI transcendental function.</summary>
    <category term="cond-mat.dis-nn" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>1998-07-21T02:15:07Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>5 pages, 1 figure, REVTeX; restriction on the parameter stressed, figure replaced, refs added (v2); typos (factors of pi) in (35), (36) corrected (v3); minor changes incl. title, version to appear in Phys.Rev.E (v4)</arxiv:comment>
